{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThree `tests/external/live_jira_cloud_mutation` files contain three audited module-docstring blocks. Their blobs and contracts were revalidated against immutable commit `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`. The later `origin/main` advance to `10533b1e3f651a60e8cea5691318c108ff1f3396` does not touch them and is irrelevant to the audit citations.\n\n## Approach and identity\nCondense only allowlisted ordinary comments and true leading docstrings. Preserve all runtime strings, prompts, fixtures, decorators, assertions, subprocess arguments, and executable behavior. Stable block IDs are `path::module-docstring`, `path::<qualified-symbol>-docstring`, or `path::<qualified-symbol>::comment(<opening words>)`; use `<module>` as the owner for module-level comments. The line spans below are immutable base citations, never the identity anchor. Adjacent blank-line cleanup is allowed only when attached to an edited block.\n\nFor each declared path, compare the immutable `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:<path>` blob directly with the final leaf commit, even if the implementation branch is based on a later main. Parse with `type_comments=True`; remove leading docstrings only from `ast.Module`, `ast.ClassDef`, `ast.FunctionDef`, and `ast.AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining AST to match. This preserves runtime strings and every executable expression. Tokenize comments and compare every matched directive-bearing physical line plus any shebang byte-for-byte. The exact leaf changed-path set (`HEAD^..HEAD`) must equal the first-class `file_impact` set.\n\n## Scope — immutable base citations\n- `_cloud_mutation_support.py:1-21` — preserve bounded blast radius, run-unique labels, primary deletion, and sweep backstops.\n- `conftest.py:1-9` — preserve explicit canary enrollment, client ownership, and cleanup role.\n- `test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py:1-20` — preserve the public-facade boundary, one-plan scope, live-write safety, and teardown guarantees.\n\nConsumers are pytest fixture discovery; the lifecycle module imports the support helper; `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` and the directory README invoke the live suite; and `tests/unit/test_external_integration_cloud_mutation_workflow.py` pins the workflow lane. No target-specific runtime docstring reader was found. Preserve `_cloud_mutation_support.py` `noqa: BLE001` directives at pinned lines 145/154 and lifecycle `noqa: E402` directives at 35-38/43 byte-for-byte; preserve exact shebang absence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes exactly the declared `file_impact` paths and only allowlisted prose blocks or their adjacent blank lines; the immutable-base normalized-AST/runtime/directive/shebang guard passes.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and retains its listed contract and real consumers; repetition, chronology, obvious narration, and ornament are removed rather than moved.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: stable block ID, immutable-before citation, final-commit citation (or `DELETED` plus surviving neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, `directives_exact`, before/after words, reviewer session, `semantic-preservation`, and `bloat-removal`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing rows, duplicate IDs, bad citations, or any non-PASS result block closure.\n- [ ] The focused hermetic checks, `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and no-timeout worktree-venv `make verify` all pass. Collection-only checks never execute live Jira mutations.\n\n## Verification\nThe authoritative executable commands and DD intent are recorded in first-class `verify_commands`. Do not replace `make verify` with `make lint`, and do not put a timeout around it.\n\nLive Jira tests are collection-only here. The five offline workflow nodes execute normally; neither live lifecycle node may execute as part of this ticket's focused verification."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788619104729259304,"uuid":"4d66635f-fea6-468c-b355-5ce103a0bb48"}